<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Castell Dinas Brân</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1260</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Dinas Bran</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Castell Dinas Brân is a ruined medieval castle on a steep hill above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llangollen">Llangollen</a> in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>. It was built around 1260 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gruffydd-maelor-i">Gruffydd ap Madog</a>, prince of Powys Fadog, on the site of an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> hillfort. Burnt by its Welsh defenders in 1277 to keep it from the English, it was never seriously reoccupied.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/castell-dinas-bran.jpg" alt="Castell Dinas Brân" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Simaron from Lower Saxony, Germany · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Above_the_Valley_(52831034885).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
